WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
A reporting workflow built around your forms and your review process.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Start with one handoff: from the technician’s record to the office’s draft.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Previous readings are a reference. They do not become today’s results.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:34.000
These sample entries will populate the draft report.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:43.000
This sample finding is a painted sprinkler in Room 214.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:50.000
The report is still a draft. It has not been approved or sent.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:59.000
Office amendments are recorded separately, with a reason for the change.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:08.000
The question goes back with the inspection, ready for the technician to answer.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:17.000
The office receives the updated field record and can review it again.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:25.000
Approving the report does not mean the deficiency has been repaired.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:32.000
One site, one system and its inspection history.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Free one-form example within 3 business days. I’ll flag complex forms up front.
